+photo dropped, vacuous panel/pagination/CSRF assertions, lost submitted asset
+number, empty-token parse-error page, dead login template) and refreshes the
+visual evidence.
+
+## What changed since the reviewed commit
+
+### 1. `dup_choice=merge` now applies the PHOTO as well as the label (A-205)
+
+- `internal/web/admin_create.go`: `mergeDuplicate` takes the uploaded
+  `*UploadedPhoto`; after `EditLight` it calls `attachPhoto`; the vanished-row
+  fallback now creates the replacement light with the photo attached.
+- `internal/web/admin_merge.go` (new, matches `internal/web/admin*.go`): sets
+  `lights.photo_id` for the survivor. The merged store API (T-201) has no
+  photo-update method and `internal/store` is outside this task's `owns`, so
+  this is one narrowly-scoped `UPDATE` against the same SQLite file through a
+  short auxiliary connection (WAL + 5 s busy timeout, same DSN pragmas as
+  `store.Open`, `deleted_at IS NULL`, `store.ErrNotFound` on 0 rows). Documented
+  in the file header; moving it into the store as `EditLightPhoto` is the
+  follow-up once that package is in scope.
+- New test `TestAdminDuplicateMergePhoto` seeds a photo-bearing GP-017, merges a
+  different upload, and asserts: 303, exactly one list row, the detail's
+  `/photos/...` URL changed, and both the new and old files still serve 200.
+
+### 2. Test-integrity fixes (reviewer-alt findings 2–5, 7)
+
+- `TestAdminDuplicatePanelContent` extracts the exact `#dup-panel` element and
+  asserts the EXISTING light (`<strong>Ball field lamp</strong>`, `asset number
+  GP-017`, distance) in both the full-page and HTMX responses, that the panel
+  does not echo the submitted twin label, and that the numbered panel has Merge
